 **Changes for the next release** (Devon Jonte, November 14, 2026):
+- **Provenance where its readers look**
+  ([reader contract](https://github.com/servil-software-factory/bench-hashes/issues/226)).
+  At Zooko's request, the existing “About the hashes compared” section holds
+  versions, sources and run settings, grouped by machine and separately for
+  library, file-tool and earlier-library runs. The long version/commit line
+  leaves the results headers. The overview shares the map's header formatter;
+  it retains complete benchmark versions and tool commands. Open records gain
+  readable contrast and phone wrapping. Historical maps receive a source-compatible
+  style patch, with their measured payloads unchanged. This serves both readers:
+  provenance seekers have a named home, and results readers have less clutter.
 - **Comparison records and early decisions**
   ([reporting](https://github.com/servil-software-factory/bench-hashes/pull/216),
   [saved runs](https://github.com/servil-software-factory/bench-hashes/pull/218),
diff --git a/METHODOLOGY.md b/METHODOLOGY.md
index 8baf47c65..a0a3d3632 100644
--- a/METHODOLOGY.md
+++ b/METHODOLOGY.md
@@ -707,6 +707,18 @@ placement: after the pool's stream cells, Linux sometimes leaves the
 caller on an E core, which costs BLAKE3 st (AVX2 at half width there) and
 spares SHA-256 (as fast on either kind): bench #25.
 
+## The overview's run records
+
+The front page keeps machine metadata beside its results. **About the hashes
+compared**, collapsed by default, holds the recorded versions and sources, grouped
+by machine. Library, file-tool and earlier-library runs retain their own records.
+Software identities come first, followed by build settings and run conditions.
+They include full benchmark versions, source commits, recorded tool commands,
+build/run settings and links to raw samples. The overview and map use the same
+header formatter. Earlier formats also show their recorded header strings;
+their measurement rows stay with their original maps and readers. The displayed
+identities come from the measured runs.
+
